<p>1.1 <strong>Organize Project Requirements</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Schedule and Milestones</strong>: Develop a timeline with key deadlines.</li>
<li><strong>Individual Logbook</strong>: Maintain detailed records of daily activities.</li>
</ul>
<p>1.2 <strong>Coordinate Project Plan</strong>: Align tasks with project goals and ensure consistency.</p>
<p>1.3 <strong>Organize Project Scope and Limitations</strong>: Define the boundaries and constraints of the project.</p>
<p>1.4 <strong>Organize Project Methodology</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sketch Project Design or Case Study</strong>: Detail the project&rsquo;s design or case study.</li>
<li><strong>Construct Design Analysis</strong>: Analyze the feasibility and performance of the design.</li>
<li><strong>Estimate Project Costs and Outcomes</strong>: Determine the financial requirements and expected results.</li>
<li><strong>Organize Needs, Equipment, Tools, and Materials</strong>: Identify and secure necessary resources for successful project completion.</li>
</ul>
